    "title": "Правила: Wish vs Hope vs Expect – Grammar Shorts",
    "level": "SHORTS",
    "overview": "Wish, hope и expect связаны с future/desired situations, но выражают разное отношение к reality.",
    "main_rule": "Hope = desired and realistically possible. Expect = believe something is likely/anticipated. Wish = unreal, unlikely or impossible situation, or regret.",
    "form": "hope + clause/to V1. expect + noun/to V1/that-clause. wish + unreal structure.",
    "when_why": "Используем, чтобы различить realistic desire, expectation и unreal/regret.",
    "examples": "I hope we can finish today. → Я надеюсь, что мы сможем закончить сегодня.\nI expect the meeting to finish at five. → Я ожидаю, что встреча закончится в пять.\nI wish I had more time. → Жаль, что у меня нет больше времени.\nI wish you were here. → Жаль, что тебя здесь нет.\nWe wish you a pleasant journey. → Желаем вам приятного путешествия.",
    "special_cases": "Wish is not a simple synonym for hope when the desired event is realistically possible.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ I wish we can finish today. → For realistic possibility: ✅ I hope we can finish today.\n❌ I expect I had more time. → For unreal present: ✅ I wish I had more time.",
    "dont_confuse": "Спроси: realistic desire → hope; likely expectation → expect; unreal/regret → wish.",
    "quick_summary": "hope = desired + possible.\nexpect = likely/anticipated.\nwish = unreal/regret.\nfixed polite: We wish you..."
  },
